## 3. The 4 Functional Capabilities

### Capability 1: Autonomous Artifact Evaluation & Quality Critique
When an artifact is generated (or upon clicking `[Evaluate Artifact]`), Addie inspects the canvas/DOM and emits a structured **Quality Scorecard**:
1. **For Canvas Games**:
   - Measures frame rate stability, canvas pixel dimensions, keydown event listeners, and collision logic.
   - Emits structured ratings: *Playability (92/100)*, *Physics Smoothness (84/100)*, *Aesthetic Harmony (90/100)*.
   - Concrete suggestion: *\"The car acceleration curve is exponential; adding linear drag dampening (0.92) will make drifting tighter. Click [Tune Physics] to apply.\"*
2. **For Interactive Websites**:
   - Inspects typography scale, button touch targets, WCAG color contrast, and layout overflow.
   - Emits critique: *\"The secondary call-to-action button has low contrast against the obsidian background. Click [Enhance Contrast] to patch.\"*
3. **For Vector SVGs**:
   - Inspects node complexity, redundant `<path>` elements, viewBox alignment, and color palette.
   - Emits critique: *\"12 redundant bezier control points detected. Click [Simplify Geometry] to reduce token size by 35%.\"*

---

### Capability 2: In-Place Page Mutation & Live Coding Agent
The Copilot acts as a live, client-side coding agent capable of mutating both the active preview sandbox and the surrounding application page:

1. **Selective In-Canvas & In-DOM Injections**:
   - *\"Нарисуй динозавра в углу\"* (Draw a dinosaur in the corner):
     - Addie synthesizes a compact vector sprite or canvas drawing routine:
       ```javascript
       // Injected by Addie In-Browser Copilot
       function drawCornerDinosaur(ctx) {
         ctx.save();
         ctx.fillStyle = '#10b981';
         // Procedural cute T-Rex silhouette in bottom-right corner
         ctx.fillRect(580, 310, 30, 30); // Body
         ctx.fillRect(595, 295, 25, 20); // Head
         ctx.fillStyle = '#ffffff';
         ctx.fillRect(610, 300, 5, 5);   // Eye
         ctx.restore();
       }
       ```
     - Injects it directly into the active animation loop without restarting the game!
2. **VFS In-Memory Patching**:
   - Modifies `/vfs/generated/` buffers via [InBrowserAddie.asl](file:///Users/purplelephant/projects/asex/asl/web/asl-src/components/InBrowserAddie.asl) action firewall.
   - Triggers `window.applyInMemoryEdits()` with zero page reload.
3. **Page-Level Styling & Theme Tweaks**:
   - *\"Сделай страницу неоновой\"* -> Modifies root CSS variables (`--color-signal: #00f0ff; --color-line: #ff005544;`).

---

### Capability 3: In-Browser Computer Use & Autonomous Navigation
Using the accessibility tree principles from [browser_cdp.asl](file:///Users/purplelephant/projects/asex/harness/src/browser_cdp.asl), Addie executes in-tab navigation and control without requiring an external OS-level Chrome process:

1. **Target Identification**:
   - Traverses the page DOM, assigning virtual accessibility indices `@e1`..`@eN` to interactive targets (Navbar links, buttons, theme toggles, article cards).
2. **Navigation Presets**:
   - `[ Go to Homepage]`: Smoothly scrolls to the top hero section (`#hero`) and updates the route hash.
   - `[ Find Latest Article]`: Navigates to the Editorial section (`#editorial`), finds the newest article card, and pulses a highlight ring around it.
   - `[ Inspect Code]`: Programmatically triggers `window.toggleCodeEditor()`, opening the in-memory VFS editor with line numbers.
   - `[ Fullscreen Sandbox]`: Calls `window.openFullscreenSandbox()` for distraction-free canvas interaction.

---

### Capability 4: Dynamic Contextual Presets (Smart Action Chips)

The preset chips automatically shift depending on the active mode:

| Active Mode | Contextual Action Chips (1-Click Execution) |
|---|---|
| **Games (`games`)** | `[ Evaluate Gameplay]` `[ Add Corner Dinosaur]` `[ Boost Game Speed]` `[ Add Sound Beeps]` `[ Reset Simulation]` |
| **Websites (`websites`)** | `[ Test Mobile Layout]` `[ Switch to Cyberpunk]` `[ Find Latest Article]` `[ Check Accessibility]` `[ Go to Homepage]` |
| **SVGs (`svgs`)** | `[ Add Neon Glow]` `[ Simplify Path Geometry]` `[ Holographic Gradient]` `[ Export ASN S-Expr]` |

---

## 4. Execution Substrate & Safety Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    UserPrompt[\"User Prompt or Preset Click\"] --> IntentRouter[\"Intent Router (Regex / Heuristic / SLM)\"]

    IntentRouter -->|Navigation / UI Control| CompUse[\"Computer Use Engine (DOM Dispatch & Scroll)\"]
    IntentRouter -->|Page Mutation / Code Patch| CodeAgent[\"In-Browser Coding Agent (VFS Mutation)\"]
    IntentRouter -->|Artifact Critique| Evaluator[\"Heuristic Quality Evaluator\"]

    CodeAgent --> Firewall[\"validate-action-firewall (InBrowserAddie.asl)\"]
    Firewall -->|Pristine Code| VFS[\"In-Memory VFS Buffer (/vfs/generated/)\"]
    VFS --> LiveSandbox[\"Active Sandbox (Iframe / Canvas)\"]

    CompUse --> PageDOM[\"Host Page DOM (Navigation & Highlights)\"]
    Evaluator --> CopilotHUD[\"Copilot Chat HUD (Scorecard & Suggestions)\"]
```

1. **Two-Tier Engine Dispatch**:
   - **Tier 0 (<10ms)**: Rule-based fast dispatcher for instant navigation (`#hero`, `#editorial`), preset mutations, and DOM highlights. Zero model invocation overhead.
   - **Tier 1 (WebGPU SLM)**: For free-form creative queries (*\"Draw a dinosaur in the corner\"*), dispatches to the in-browser WebWorker running Qwen 2.5 Coder 0.5B/1.5B via WebGPU.
2. **Security & Sandbox Firewall**:
   - All generated code passes through `validate-action-firewall` in [InBrowserAddie.asl](file:///Users/purplelephant/projects/asex/asl/web/asl-src/components/InBrowserAddie.asl#L60).
   - Blocks any attempt to touch `document.cookie`, `localStorage`, or external network endpoints.
   - Canvas animations run inside bounded `requestAnimationFrame` loops with frame drop protection.

